    ["Position recognition","ALIGN","Optical position detection before every placement. Exact positioning of the individual sheets is <em>the</em> central quality criterion for this station."],
    ["Vacuum gripper","PLACE","Grippers of different sizes handle anode and cathode. Stacking accuracy ±200–300 µm."],
    ["Z-folding","WEAVE","The classic variant: the separator is folded into a Z and sheets are inserted alternately from left and right. The tape is cut only after stacking finishes."],
    ["Finished stack","OUTPUT","Up to 120 layers, fixed with adhesive tape. Anode tabs to one side, cathode tabs to the other."]],
  params:["Z-folding: sheets placed laterally into the folded separator web","Single-sheet stacking: separator supplied as a sheet","Stacking accuracy ±200 µm – 300 µm","≈1 s per sheet"],
  alts:["Lamination — electrode and separator laminated continuously, then hot pressed","Pocket stacking — cathode placed in a separator pocket, then anodes alternately"],
  qInf:["Position detection and alignment of different sheet sizes with a vacuum gripper","Mechanical pre-tensioning of the separator"],
  qFeat:["Positioning accuracy of anode and cathode sheets","Damage-free electrode surfaces and edges","Avoidance of electrostatic charging"],
  sop:["Verify dew point and static control","Load magazines, confirm polarity per side","Calibrate vision to the sheet datum","Set separator pre-tension","Stack and verify layer count","Tape the stack and hand over"] },

{ id:"winding", no:"08", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Winding", machine:"winding", routes:"cyl prism",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"dry, −40…−50 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 15–35 M", takt:"up to 30 cells/min (cyl)",
  purpose:"Wind anode, cathode and two separators into a jelly roll — the cylindrical and prismatic route.",
  inp:"Daughter rolls, 4 webs", out:"Jelly roll, taped",
  parts:[
    ["Four webs","FEED","Cathode, anode and two separator webs are drawn off together. The sequence is the same as the stacking order, just continuous."],
    ["Winding mandrel","WIND","A centre pin for cylindrical cells, a flat mandrel for prismatic. The flat mandrel is the only reason a prismatic jelly roll is prismatic."],
    ["Taping","FIX","An adhesive strip secures the final turn so the roll cannot unwind during handling."],
    ["Jelly roll","OUTPUT","Up to 30 cells/min cylindrical, up to 6 cells/min prismatic. Tab welding is often integrated into the winder for cylindrical cells."]],
  params:["Up to 30 cells/min (cylindrical)","Up to 6 cells/min (prismatic)","Tab welding integrated in the cylindrical winder"],
  alts:["Reference route shown; equipment configuration varies by manufacturer"],
  qInf:["Winding speed","Web tension","Web edge control","Avoidance of electrostatic charging"],
  qFeat:["Positioning accuracy of anode and cathode foils","Damage-free electrode surfaces and edges"],
  sop:["Thread all four webs and confirm the order","Set individual web tensions","Check edge alignment on the first roll","Confirm tab weld position","Verify roll diameter and tape","Transfer without radial load"] },

{ id:"packPouch", no:"09", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Packaging — pouch", machine:"packPouch", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"dry, −40…−50 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 16–23 M", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Weld the tabs, put the stack into deep-drawn aluminium composite foil and seal three of the four sides.",
  inp:"Taped stack", out:"Pouch cell, one side open",
  parts:[
    ["Deep drawing","FORM","The pouch foil — polyamide / aluminium / polypropylene composite — is drawn up to 6 mm deep to make the cavity. Done in line or bought pre-drawn."],
    ["Tab welding","JOIN","All anode current collectors are welded together and to the negative tab, all cathode collectors to the positive tab. Ultrasonic welding at roughly 15–40 kHz, or laser."],
    ["Insertion","LOAD","The stack is placed into the deep-drawn cavity."],
    ["Partial sealing","SEAL","Three sides are sealed gas-tight by impulse or contact sealing. The rule of thumb on the shop floor: 1 mm of seal seam ≈ one year of cell life. One side is left open for filling."]],
  params:["Deep drawing up to 6 mm","Ultrasonic welding ≈15–40 kHz","Aluminium composite film: polyamide / aluminium / polypropylene","1 mm seam ≈ 1 year of cell lifetime"],
  alts:["Book folding — one foil with two drawn cavities, folded like a book and sealed"],
  qInf:["Reduction of thermal stress during contacting and sealing","Seal seam width","Sealing temperature and pressure"],
  qFeat:["Low contact resistance, low mechanical and thermal stress at the weld","Fatigue strength and tightness of the sealing seams"],
  sop:["Verify foil lot and draw depth","Set sonotrode energy for the collector stack thickness","Weld and pull-test a sample","Insert the stack without abrading the foil","Seal three sides to the seam-width spec","Leak-check before release"] },

{ id:"packHard", no:"09", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Packaging — can", machine:"packHard", routes:"cyl prism",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"dry, −40…−50 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 10–20 M", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Insert the jelly roll into a metal can, insulate it, and weld the terminals and the lid.",
  inp:"Jelly roll", out:"Sealed can, fill port open",
  parts:[
    ["Jelly roll with terminals","INPUT","For prismatic cells the roll edges are compressed, fixed and ultrasonically welded to the contact terminals on the lid."],
    ["Insulator foil","INSULATE","An insulation foil protects the jelly roll during insertion and keeps it off the metal housing."],
    ["Lid welding","SEAL","The housing is sealed by laser welding. Flexible beam guidance and beam shaping are needed for the prismatic lid geometry."],
    ["Cylindrical route","VARIANT","A bottom insulator goes in first, then the roll. The anode collector is resistance-welded to the can bottom; the cathode collector is laser-welded to the lid. An insulation ring finishes the job."]],
  params:["Ultrasonic welding ≈15–40 kHz","Flexible laser beam guidance for the prismatic lid","Anode-to-housing: resistance welding","Cathode-to-lid: laser welding"],
  alts:["Reference route shown; equipment configuration varies by manufacturer"],
  qInf:["Reduction of thermal stress during welding","Purity of the metallic housing","Handling of the jelly roll"],
  qFeat:["Low contact resistance, low mechanical and thermal stress","Insulation against the metallic housing"],
  sop:["Check can and insulator cleanliness","Compress and weld the roll to the terminals","Insert with the insulator in place","Weld the lid and inspect the seam","Verify insulation resistance","Leave the fill port open"] },

{ id:"fillPouch", no:"10", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Electrolyte filling — pouch", machine:"fillPouch", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"extra dry, −50…−70 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 6–12 M", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Dose electrolyte into the cell under vacuum, then drive it into every pore before sealing.",
  inp:"Open pouch cell", out:"Filled cell with gas bag",
  parts:[
    ["Filling under vacuum","DOSE","The chamber is evacuated to roughly 0.01 mbar before a high-precision dosing needle meters the electrolyte. The very dry environment limits LiPF₆ hydrolysis and the formation of HF-containing species that can degrade interfaces and cell life."],
    ["Wetting by pressure cycling","WET","Filling and wetting are two different sub-processes. Inert gas pressure and vacuum are alternated so capillary action pulls electrolyte into the pores. The cycle is repeated several times."],
    ["Seal under vacuum","CLOSE","The last side is sealed under vacuum. A gas bag — dead space — is left attached to catch the gas that formation will produce."]],
  params:["Vacuum-chamber evacuation ≈0.01 mbar","Wetting-cycle pressure reference ≈150 mbar","Consistent, continuous or cyclic filling","Very dry environment necessary","Gravimetric control of the electrolyte quantity"],
  alts:["Reference route shown; equipment configuration varies by manufacturer"],
  qInf:["Dosing method","Geometry and closing mechanism of the dosing needle","Electrolyte transport system — piping"],
  qFeat:["Dosing and distribution accuracy","No electrolyte residue in the sealing seam","Tightness of the sealed cell"],
  sop:["Confirm dew point and HF exposure controls","Verify needle geometry and dose by weight","Evacuate, dose, pressurise, repeat","Check for residue in the seal area","Seal under vacuum with the gas bag attached","Weigh the cell to confirm the electrolyte quantity"] },

{ id:"fillHard", no:"10", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Electrolyte filling — can", machine:"fillHard", routes:"cyl prism",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"extra dry, −50…−70 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 12–18 M", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Fill the sealed can through its port, wet the roll, then close the cell permanently.",
  inp:"Welded can, port open", out:"Sealed filled cell",
  parts:[
    ["Prismatic fill valve","DOSE","Electrolyte goes in through a valve in the lid, under vacuum, by dosing needle."],
    ["Cylindrical fill","DOSE","Filled through the open end before the cell is closed."],
    ["Valve sealing","CLOSE","The prismatic fill valve is laser-sealed once wetting is complete."],
    ["Beading and crimping","CLOSE","Cylindrical cells are closed mechanically: a bead is rolled into the can and the top is crimped over a gasket."]],
  params:["Vacuum-chamber evacuation ≈0.01 mbar","Wetting-cycle pressure reference ≈150 mbar","Consistent, continuous or cyclic filling","Very dry environment necessary","Gravimetric control of the electrolyte quantity"],
  alts:["Reference route shown; equipment configuration varies by manufacturer"],
  qInf:["Dosing method","Geometry and closing mechanism of the dosing needle","Electrolyte transport system"],
  qFeat:["Dosing and distribution accuracy","Tightness of the sealed cell","Electrolyte quantity"],
  sop:["Confirm dew point and HF controls","Dose by weight through the port","Cycle pressure to wet the roll","Seal the valve or bead and crimp","Leak-test every cell","Clean any external residue"] },

{ id:"rollpress", no:"11", phase:"Cell finishing", title:"Roll pressing", machine:"rollpress", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"Normal factory air", dew:"not controlled", temp:"22 ± 3 °C"}, cost:"€ 5–15 M", takt:"2–5 s per cell",
  purpose:"Squeeze the filled pouch cell between rollers so electrolyte reaches every corner of every electrode sheet.",
  inp:"Filled pouch cell", out:"Evenly wetted cell",
  parts:[
    ["Good carrier","HOLD","A gripper clamps the cell into a dedicated carrier that stays with it through finishing."],
    ["Roller pair","PRESS","A servo motor guides the cell through two rollers at a defined pressure. Pressure must be even across the whole cell surface."],
    ["Cleaning rollers","CLEAN","The rollers are cleaned between cells so nothing is pressed into the pouch foil."],
    ["Result","EFFECT","More uniform electrolyte distribution reduces poorly wetted or locally inactive regions and supports more uniform formation. The benefit depends on cell design and the full formation protocol."]],
  params:["Defined pressure","Homogeneous pressure over the entire cell surface","2–5 s per cell","Ideal coverage of the individual electrode sheets"],
  alts:["A vibrating table is used instead for prismatic and cylindrical cells"],
  qInf:["Pressure distribution","Roller geometry","Process control — number of passes"],
  qFeat:["Optimum SEI formation in the next step","Electrolyte distribution within the cell","Capacity of the cell after formation"],
  sop:["Clamp the cell in its carrier","Set pressure and pass count","Confirm roller cleanliness","Run passes and inspect the pouch surface","Check for seam stress","Release to formation"] },

{ id:"formation", no:"12", phase:"Cell finishing", title:"Formation", machine:"formation", routes:ALL,
  env:{iso:"Normal factory air", dew:"not controlled", temp:"22 ± 3 °C"}, cost:"€ 65–95 M in the reference guide — one of the most capital-intensive stages", takt:"up to 15 h",
  purpose:"Give the cell its first controlled charge and discharge cycles, which build the SEI and turn the materials into their working form.",
  inp:"Filled, wetted cell", out:"Activated cell with a formed SEI",
  parts:[
    ["Formation rack","CONTACT","Cells sit in good carriers in racks and are contacted by spring-loaded pins. Low contact resistance at those pins is a named requirement — a bad contact falsifies the measurement and heats the tab."],
    ["Charge / discharge profile","CYCLE","First charge at roughly 0.1–0.5 C between about 20% and 80% SOC, with the C-rate stepped up on each successive cycle. Up to 24 hours in total."],
    ["Product carrier","PRESSURE","Top view: cells are held and, for pouch cells in particular, lightly pressurised during formation. Orientation, contact method, temperature and pressure all influence the result."],
    ["SEI and gas","CHEMISTRY","Lithium moves into the graphite and the solid electrolyte interphase forms on its surface. The reaction consumes lithium and generates gas — which is why the gas bag is there."]],
  params:["First charge ≈0.1–0.5 C, SOC ≈20–80%","C-rate increased with each successive cycle","Duration up to 24 h","Low contact resistance at the spring-loaded pins"],
  alts:["Procedures differ by manufacturer and cell chemistry — formation recipes are treated as core know-how"],
  qInf:["Orientation of the cells","Contact method","Process temperature","Pressurisation, especially for pouch cells"],
  qFeat:["Formation of the SEI layer","Stability of the SEI layer","Internal resistance of the cell"],
  sop:["Load carriers and verify every pin contact","Select the formation recipe for the chemistry","Run the stepped C-rate profile","Log current, voltage and temperature per cell","Watch for outliers against the fleet","Release to degassing or aging"] },

